    "final_answer": "I have all the information I need. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n## Answer\n\nThe open-source repository I found that is focused on natural language processing in Ruby and updated within the last week is:\n\n### **moznion/neologdish-normalizer-ruby**\n🔗 **URL:** https://github.com/moznion/neologdish-normalizer-ruby\n\n**Details:**\n- **Description:** A Japanese text normalization library for Ruby that follows the conventions of neologd, with some performance optimizations, without external dependencies\n- **Language:** Ruby (99.3%)\n- **License:** MIT license (open-source)\n- **Topics:** ruby, nlp, normalization, neologd\n- **Last Updated:** **Yesterday** (within the last week) — verified through GitHub search results and the branches page which shows several renovate[bot] branches updated 2 days ago\n- **Stars:** 1 (a relatively new repo)\n- **Releases:** 3 total, latest v0.2.0\n\n**Why it matches:**\n1. ✅ **Open-source** (MIT licensed)\n2. ✅ **Focused on NLP in Ruby** — Japanese text normalization is a core NLP preprocessing task, following the well-known neologd (Neologism Dictionary for Japanese) conventions\n3. ✅ **Updated within the last week** — both GitHub search and the branches activity log confirm updates 2 days ago by the renovate[bot] dependency management bot, plus an \"Updated yesterday\" timestamp in search results\n\nThis is a perfect match for all the task requirements: an actively maintained, open-source Ruby NLP library updated within the last 7 days.",
